{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And Elohim blessed them.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory said that they needed a blessing because human beings hunt and eat them. And the reason He did not likewise bless the plants and the trees — seeing that they too are surely a blessing for human beings, and it is written of them (Leviticus 25:21): ״וצויתי את ברכתי לכם בשנה הששית״ — if so, why did He not bless them? It may be said that all living creatures were created male and female, in the likeness of man; therefore He blessed them, that the species should multiply and reproduce one from another. But the plants that sprouted upon the face of the earth, though very numerous, had no need for a blessing. And the reason He did not bless the beasts and the wild animals on the sixth day is that from this blessing of the fish and the birds — which are from the waters — the sentient creatures of the earth were also blessed, for all non-speaking living creatures are of one way. And you should know that by the power of this blessing the fish endured and were not obliterated by the decree of the Flood, as our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded of (Genesis 7:22): ״מכל אשר בחרבה מתו״ — but not the fish of the sea; for all the trees and plants were obliterated, and every living creature from man to beast. And further, we may understand from the power of this blessing — which He mentioned as פרו ורבו for fish and birds — that fish and birds do not reproduce at fixed seasons, but throughout all the seasons of the year they are fruitful and multiply and reproduce one from another, unlike trees and plants, and unlike beasts and wild animals, which He did not bless explicitly, for they do not produce fruit or give birth except at fixed seasons of the year."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:27:16.618877243Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}